   Regenerated deterministically from disk. Validation vs the last VALID feat version (12dd54eb7): 0 files
   wrongly dropped; +21 files correctly RECOVERED (TOUSettingsModal/DashboardSettingsModal/EntryDrawer/
   Drawer/Modal/Popover/AcknowledgeAlertDialog/GeofenceDrawer/NotificationBellPopover logic that the feat
   commit had silently lost) + my 3 AnnouncerRegion logic files. Headless test count rose accordingly
   (~17.7k -> 18075), i.e. ~300 previously-dropped tests are now compiled and run again.

2. CS0266 compile error in modals-dialogs/EntryDrawer/EntryDrawer.cs and
   modals-dialogs/FlagEditDrawer/FlagEditDrawer.cs: bare "DrawerSide.Right" resolved to the
   same-namespace ModalsDialogs.DrawerSide (introduced later by Drawer/Drawer.Model.cs) instead of the
   Components.UI.DrawerSide that TsDrawer.Side expects. The failed C# compile starved the XAML compiler,
   surfacing as a cascade of WMC0001/WMC0110 + a WMC9999 internal crash on UNRELATED types (TsButton,
   TsRouteAnnouncer, ...). Fixed by qualifying the enum to Components.UI.DrawerSide.Right in those two
   files (1 token each; identical enum shape; no behaviour change). Confirmed pre-existing (reproduced with
   my surface files moved aside) and NOT caused by the surface.

